        "final_disposition": "already-adapted",
        "reason": "The complete two-file/five-hunk attachment change is present in the owned legacy trigger. The four trigger hunks capture the required-selection value only on a genuine overlay attachment, before subsequent input, and preserve it through repeated open calls and option-list hide/reshow. The fifth hunk corrects an API-guard comment and does not change a public signature. Existing named native tests require retained model/selection while typing, one chosen-value publication, one unmatched-text reset after filtering and safe closure with no options. Current whole-method Forms/RxJS diagnostics support this source judgment; actual Angular DI/rendering, packed behavior and runtime/compiler/RxJS/peer floors remain separate mandatory executions.",
