        "bucket": "behavior-semantic",
        "subject": "fix(material/autocomplete): clear selected option if it is removed while typing (#28146)",
        "files": [
          "src/material/autocomplete/autocomplete-trigger.ts",
          "src/material/autocomplete/autocomplete.spec.ts"
        ],
        "final_disposition": "already-adapted",
        "reason": "The complete two-file/three-hunk typing/reset change is present in the owned legacy trigger. Optional nonempty typing quietly deselects a selected option when its displayed value no longer matches; displayWith receives the selected option value, retaining the correction to the original intermediate object argument. Required selection remains selected while typing until choice or dismissal. Programmatic cleanup is keyed to a nullish model, preserving non-null falsy values. The strengthened existing native cases require required-selection retention/reset, direct nonempty typing with display callback identity and quiet deselection, and reactive selected-state cleanup. Current whole-method Forms/RxJS diagnostics support this source judgment; actual Angular DI/rendering, packed behavior and runtime/compiler/RxJS/peer floors remain separate mandatory executions.",
